      "units": [
        {
          "id": "ec2v6-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Let's put an inventory app on Amazon E C two. E C two gives you an on-demand virtual server when you need control of the operating system and installed software.",
          "text_sha256": "a44a8151795b5533147cea8e7c51674cb4eae1a320b3f0891d655be877922499",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a88a24aad58a73d31477ad404b94f535ef58adf644d67a341fb7c9fb77814484",
          "asset_sha256": "ee985647f83a96e2f23ec3944c318983a8c0744ccbb7b1f8e99fc948dfc8a426"
        },
        {
          "id": "ec2v6-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "First, pick a starting image. An Amazon Machine Image, or A M I, supplies the operating system and any bundled software. Here, that starting system is Amazon Linux.",
          "text_sha256": "0dea181ee7a01c423100cc29ff40daa3582acc1e535268714950c38fe32430fa",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "05c50ce18c9e669d5c89feef40e9c0d5e53fef22c92e63ecc937dcf331217310",
          "asset_sha256": "ee985647f83a96e2f23ec3944c318983a8c0744ccbb7b1f8e99fc948dfc8a426"
        },
        {
          "id": "ec2v6-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Then size the server. The instance type determines how much C P U and memory the app can use. This example starts with two virtual C P U’s and eight gibibytes of memory.",
          "text_sha256": "3f64bf82c616b3b001efb12172001442341bb9c94a9774d44ece039fdf6912ab",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "bf98a3b8bdfa7fc8af6e922526674d1ef7aca1393f7955f15abdbba75c6097cf",
          "asset_sha256": "ee985647f83a96e2f23ec3944c318983a8c0744ccbb7b1f8e99fc948dfc8a426"
        },
        {
          "id": "ec2v6-04",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Launch the instance and run the app. Its security group allows H T T P S from office I P addresses. An attached E B S volume keeps the app's files when you stop and start the instance.",
          "text_sha256": "1e092519ea2a10cbe997d1649cc595bb66c377580c7db6f8d65e746cb3223437",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d63f99f8f5528af2fd5d39356cee890949a1ef0cd4f45d353e349790a4012e65",
          "asset_sha256": "ee985647f83a96e2f23ec3944c318983a8c0744ccbb7b1f8e99fc948dfc8a426"
        },
        {
          "id": "ec2v6-05",
          "slide": 5,
          "text": "Now staff can open the inventory in a browser and check stock. A W S runs the physical hardware. You still patch the guest operating system and manage the app.",
          "text_sha256": "21cecf12ac916779253fd5f74bf0eec9e8bccd8dd94de2a84cdd69c687bc55f1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "04067600ccbd253d5f873300ccc775f482a3da73be61a42e554b1075ed93fe66",
          "asset_sha256": "ee985647f83a96e2f23ec3944c318983a8c0744ccbb7b1f8e99fc948dfc8a426"
        }
      ]
    }
